  "reading": "The other detectors truncate each document to their input limit and read Fast-DetectGPT 61,440, Desklib v1.01 92,160, ModernBERT RAID+MAGE (Drayson) 61,440, e5-small-lora 61,440, Binoculars 61,440 tokens in all; Litmus's engine read every token of every document, 595,890 tokens. The figures say what each detector's GPU did while it read its own share, not that they read the same text.",
  "windows": "Reading took (Fast-DetectGPT 14.7 s, 64 polls; Desklib v1.01 5.7 s, 25 polls; ModernBERT RAID+MAGE (Drayson) 1.4 s, 8 polls; e5-small-lora 0.9 s, 7 polls; Binoculars 4.6 s, 23 polls), so a mean busy time rests on the polls named.",
